# Backend architecture

Four projects under `seeka-backend/`, one per Löwy layer. Project references
enforce the direction, and `ArchitectureTests` enforces the call rules.

```
Seeka.Api (Client)  -->  Seeka.Managers  -->  Seeka.Engines
Seeka.ResourceAccess  -->  Seeka.Managers (access interfaces), Seeka.Engines
Seeka.Api  -->  Seeka.ResourceAccess   (composition root only)
```

| Layer | Project | Folders | Never |
|---|---|---|---|
| Client | `Seeka.Api` | `Controllers/<Area>Controller.cs`, `Http/` (edge policy, exception handler, claims) | Inject accessors or engines, run queries, decide policy |
| Manager | `Seeka.Managers` | `<Area>/<Area>Manager.cs`, `Contracts/<Area>/` (requests, views), `Access/<Accessor>/` (interfaces and their records) | Reference EF, ASP.NET, Npgsql, or Hangfire, or call another manager |
| Engine | `Seeka.Engines` | `Eligibility/`, `Matching/`, `Outreach/`, `Intake/`, `Pipeline/`, `Accounts/` (`PhoneNumberPolicy`) | Do I/O, reference any other Seeka project |
| ResourceAccess | `Seeka.ResourceAccess` | `Accessors/`, `Persistence/` (`SeekaDbContext`, `Entities/`, `Migrations/`), `Mapping/`, `BackgroundJobs/` | Hold business rules, call another accessor |

## Call rules (closed)

- A controller depends only on managers. It calls one manager method per request and passes `User.RequireUserId()`, never a workspace ID.
- A manager sequences one use case: resolve the workspace (`memberships.RequireWorkspaceAsync`), load through accessors, ask engines, save through one accessor call. It never calls another manager.
- An engine is pure policy: static, deterministic, and testable with no host or database. It never calls an accessor.
- An accessor does one atomic reach into a resource with a business verb (`SaveImportAsync`, `ChangeStageAsync`), not CRUD (`Update<T>`). It returns `Contracts` or `Access` records, never EF entities, and owns its transaction.
- Accessors are the repositories: one interface per accessor in `Seeka.Managers/Access/`, implemented `internal sealed` in `Seeka.ResourceAccess/Accessors/`. No generic `IRepository<T>`.
- Reads go through managers too.

## Managers by volatility

| Manager | Owns | Changes when |
|---|---|---|
| `MembershipManager` | register, sign in and out, session, candidate setup | onboarding and search intent change |
| `JobSearchManager` | import, pipeline, job detail, stage, activity | sourcing and fit verdicts change |
| `OutreachManager` | contacts, drafts, draft edits | insider discovery and tailoring change |

Add a method to the manager that owns the volatility. Add a new manager only for a new kind of change, not for a new noun.

## Where new code goes

- New policy (scoring, verdicts, normalization that decides identity): an engine in `Seeka.Engines/<Area>/`.
- New external provider (OpenAI, enrichment, ATS): an interface in `Seeka.Managers/Access/<Provider>/`, implemented in `Seeka.ResourceAccess/Accessors/`.
- New HTTP route: an action on the controller for that manager, with `[HttpGet]`, `[HttpPost]`, and so on. No `Map*` minimal endpoints. Every route is under the global rate limit in `Http/ApiRateLimits` (per user ID when signed in, else per IP); credential endpoints also carry `[EnableRateLimiting(ApiRateLimits.Auth)]`. `UseAuthentication()` must stay before `UseRateLimiter()`.
- One top-level type per file. The file name matches the type.

```csharp
// ❌ Controller reaches past the manager
public JobsController(IJobAccess jobs) { ... }

// ✅ Controller calls one manager; the manager resolves the workspace
public JobsController(JobSearchManager jobSearch) { ... }
await jobSearch.FindJobAsync(User.RequireUserId(), savedJobId, ct);
```

## Errors

- `ArgumentException` → 400, `UnauthorizedAccessException` → 401, `InvalidOperationException` → 409. Mapped in `Http/SeekaExceptionHandler`.
- Not found is a `null` or `false` return that the controller turns into 404.

## Tests

- Engines: plain unit tests.
- Managers: unit tests with fakes from `seeka-backend.Tests/Fakes/`.
- Accessors: tests against the EF in-memory provider or PostgreSQL.
- `ArchitectureTests` must stay green. Do not weaken a rule to make a change pass. Move the code instead.
